      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0",
      "artist": "John Allan",
      "description": "Staigue stone fort Staigue stone fort is a round stone iron-age fort near Sneem, probably built as a defensive stronghold for a local leader and his clan.\nThe walls are over 5m high in places, and up to 4m thick. It is an impressive construction, built without any sort of mortar.",
